From 8ea8348ef1970b3793f61744c1177d84f1bea4b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kirn Gill II <segin2005@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 20:26:08 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] LE: header, objects, names, entry table, fixups; VxD DDB and
 INT 20h service IDs; W3 modules

Parse the Linear Executable format (LE; LX headers too, without loading LX
pages): the header (fixed: the data pages offset at 0x80 was missing, and the
module flag bits), the object table and object page table, resident and
non-resident names, the entry table, imported modules, and the fixup page
and record tables (-v lists every record). For Windows VxDs, print the
Device Descriptor Block found through the *_DDB export, with its pointers
resolved through the internal fixups, and with -s the dynamic-link service
IDs that follow INT 20h in executable objects. For W3 files (WIN386.EXE),
dump each module in the W3 table (-m selects one).

Sources: IBM's LX format description, the Windows 3.1 DDK's documentation
of the DDB and of the INT 20h dynamic-link convention; checked against the
Windows 3.1 VxDs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 README.md |   4 +-
 le.h      | 278 +++++++++++++++++-------
 readexe.c | 638 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
